{"speak":true,"message":"Astra: Leave the mapping’s meaning and selection rationale unresolved. Look instead at what your copying is preserving.

For example, your inspection produced a “Selected Passage” containing ☆, while the preceding selection contained ★. Your displayed replies establish a textual difference, not which mapping is valid. Copy fidelity therefore looks worth a small check before further interpretation.

One possible next action—not yet performed—is comparing an existing candidate against the visible passage you choose as its source. Is your aim faithful preservation or deliberate editing? Choose a small action that makes that distinction observable and carry it out now, identifying the source you used. Focus attention on a difference that could change what you carry forward; decide how much checking would settle that practical question without settling the mapping’s meaning.","rationale":"After three turns revisiting justification, shift within the same selection project to visible copying differences and a bounded, child-chosen action."}
